# Orbinum Testnet — relayer stack.
#
# The Tesseract signers do NOT live here: it does not expand environment variables in its
# config, so they go directly in `relayer.toml` (copied from relayer.toml.example).

# ── Tesseract ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This stack no longer runs a node. Tesseract reads Orbinum over the network from an
# ARCHIVE node — see relayer.toml.example for which one and why.
#
# The node that used to live here ran `--state-pruning 1000`, on the reasoning that
# GRANDPA proving only needs justifications and headers. True for consensus, false for
# messaging: `ismp_queryEvents` re-executes the runtime at each block to read
# `System::Events` (cleared every block), so a state-pruned node returns an empty list
# with NO error. Consensus flowed while every ISMP message was silently dropped.
#
# The RPC endpoints are NOT set here: Tesseract does not expand environment variables in
# its config, so they are written literally in relayer.toml.
TESSERACT_MEM_LIMIT=2g
TESSERACT_CPUS=1.0
